==Galician==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|gl|cozer||reinteg}}

===Etymology===
{{inh+|gl|roa-opt|cozer}} (13th century, ''{{w|Cantigas de Santa Maria}}''), from {{inh|gl|LL.|coco|cocere}}, from {{inh|gl|la|coquo|coquere}}. Cognate with {{cog|pt|cozer}} and {{cog|es|cocer}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{gl-pr|cȯcêr}}
* {{hyph|gl|co|cer}}

===Verb===
{{gl-verb}}

# to [[boil]], [[stew]]
#: {{syn|gl|ferver}}
#* {{quote-book|gl|year=1409|editor=J. L. Pensado Tomé|title=Tratado de Albeitaria|location=Santiago de Compostela|publisher=Centro Ramón Piñeiro|page=131|text=pisa moy ben todo con exulla uedra de porco et faz ende hũa masa et '''coze''' todo con uyno, meyxeo ameude ataa que se '''coza''' ben|t=pound it carefully with old pork lard and make a dough with it and '''boil''' everything in wine, stir it frequently till it is well '''cooked'''}}
# to [[cook]]
#: {{syn|gl|cociñar}}
#* {{quote-book|gl|year=c. 1300|editor=R. Martínez López|title=General Estoria. Versión gallega del siglo XIV|location=Oviedo|publisher=Publicacións de Archivum|page=89|text=Et estes omẽs yam comendo as carnes ja et os peyxes et pescados que achauam et matauã elles os que podiam prender; pero nõ os '''coziã''' que nõ [sabiam] ajnda amaneyra delo, mays enxugauam aquelas carnes et peyxes ao sol|t=And these people were eating the meats and seafood and fish that they can find and kill and catch; but they did not '''cook''' them, because they still did not know the way, but they dried these meats and seafood in the sun}}
# to [[bake]]
#: {{syn|gl|enfornar}}
#: {{ux|gl|Maruxiña da Forneira / se é que '''coces''' faime un bolo / se mo fas faimo de trigo / que o centeo non cho como|Little Mary of the Baker / if you bake make a loaf for me / and if you make it, make it wheat / because I don't eat rye|q=traditional song}}
#* {{quote-book|gl|year=c. 1300|editor=R. Martínez López|title=General Estoria. Versión gallega del siglo XIV|location=Oviedo|publisher=Publicacións de Archivum|page=206|text=fezo '''cozer''' pera elles pã çençeno|t=She ordered to '''bake''' rye bread for them}}
# to [[fire]]
#: {{syn|gl|enfornar}}
#* {{quote-book|gl|year=1484|editor=X. Ferro Couselo|title=A vida e a fala dos devanceiros. Escolma de documentos en galego dos séculos XIII ao XVI|location=Vigo|publisher=Galaxia|page=445|text=cinco mil ladrillos ben '''cozidos''' e de boo barro|t=five thousand bricks, correctly '''fired''' and made of good clay}}
# {{lb|gl|flax processing}} to [[ret]]
# {{lb|gl|wine processing}} to [[ferment]]
#: {{syn|gl|fermentar}}
# to [[digest]]
#: {{syn|gl|dixerir}}

