==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ang|cocur}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|ang|gmw-pro|*kokar}}, whence also {{cog|ofs|koker}}, {{cog|osx|kokar}} ({{cog|nl|koker}}), {{cog|goh|kohhār}} ({{cog|de|Köcher}}). The origin of the West Germanic word is unknown, but note that a similar word can be found in Turkic and Mongolic languages: see {{cog|xgn-pro|*kökexür}} for more.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|cocer}}

===Noun===
